      "writtenOn": "2026-09-07T05:49:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Did we consider reusing the `executeCmd` utility API implementation at https://github.com/openbmc/openpower-vpd-parser/blob/2c7847513f76ef9042b5c4ef98711e5e41945994/vpd-manager/include/utility/common_utility.hpp#L114 ?\n\nDoes this new implementation have any benefits over the existing implementation?",
      "revId": "137a8c0b67016d8c0378fd8dd6096d8f1e63e01c",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ef655889_ccf21268",
        "filename": "vpd-tool/include/tool_utils.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 1312,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-07T08:56:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The main functional improvement is that the new implementation can distinguish between successfully creating the pipe and the actual command succeeding. The existing implementation does not check the command\u0027s exit status.\n\nIt also uses `std::expected` for cleaner error handling.",
      "parentUuid": "ca311682_73a26d64",
      "revId": "137a8c0b67016d8c0378fd8dd6096d8f1e63e01c",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
