      "writtenOn": "2026-09-07T09:20:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "fgets returns nullptr for both end-of-file and a read error. A read error on the pipe is silently treated as end-of-file, and partial/empty output is then passed to the caller.\n\n\n\n```suggestion\n      while (fgets(l_buffer, sizeof(l_buffer), l_pipe.get()) !\u003d nullptr)\n        // After the loop, call ferror(l_pipe.get()) and return an error code if it is set:\n\nif (ferror(l_pipe.get()))\n{\n    std::cerr \u003c\u003c std::format(\"Read error while capturing output of [{}].\", i_command) \u003c\u003c std::endl;\n    pclose(l_pipe.release());\n    return std::unexpected(ErrorCode::SYS_CMD_FAILED);\n}\n```",
      "revId": "137a8c0b67016d8c0378fd8dd6096d8f1e63e01c",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
